{
  "schema": "loom.runtime_profile/1",
  "domain": "free_providers",
  "revision": 2,
  "description": "Model sources for guests (R103 §4, B1). Every entry is DATA and a preset: providers, models, limits and data terms are dated observations (observed_at, source_url, source_rating) to refresh, never rules. An entry is used only when enabled is true and its condition holds (active_when key_present = its auth_env name is present in the operator's keys file, server_accounts guests.keys_file; the key goes to the guest runtime in memory through credential_overlay and never into the guest directory). disabled_reason says why an entry is out of the guest queue on the operator's key and since when (provider terms are treated like law: a closed choice with a reason and a date). data_terms.summary (pl/en) is shown to the guest before the first send and copied into every receipt (provider_terms). budget on a paid entry is a spending preset (EUR per day/week, share of each credit, advisory threshold). free_model_choice.tier_order (R103 B3) = sources of these tiers are tried first, in this order, then by quality (preset: free keys before the operator's paid credits; empty = quality only); free_model_choice: which model a guest without his own key gets; table = an example ranking with dates (quality 0..1), require = data-terms condition on the operator's key, reevaluate = when the choice is computed again (B1 computes it when the guest runtime opens; per_message comes with the quota counters of B4). active_when service_account (R103 B3) = a short-lived OAuth access token of the machine's service account from the metadata server (auth.metadata_base, refreshed auth.refresh_before_seconds before expiry, memory only; {project} in base_url comes from the metadata server unless project is set). pricing = dated price per million tokens with its source (to_eur = dated conversion), used with the provider's usage for the spend counter (accounts root guest_spend.json, numbers only; GET /api/pool/summary spend). exhaustion_markers = text in a provider error that means exhausted (429, quota); the provider is then skipped for exhausted_cooldown_seconds and the guest is switched by fallback order, told in model_source.switched (R103 §4.4). data_terms_prompt = when the guest is asked before sending (first_use, every_session, every_message; never only for his own key). test_providers: extra entries an operator overlay may add (tests use a mock).",
  "defaults": {
    "providers": [
      {
        "id": "groq",
        "display_name": "Groq",
        "base_url": "https://api.groq.com/openai/v1",
        "adapter": "openai_compatible",
        "auth_env": "GROQ_API_KEY",
        "auth_secret": "api_key",
        "tier": "free",
        "active_when": "key_present",
        "enabled": true,
        "models": [
          {
            "id": "openai/gpt-oss-120b",
            "notes": "przykład / example"
          },
          {
            "id": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile",
            "notes": "przykład / example"
          }
        ],
        "limits": {
          "rpm": 30,
          "rpd": 1000,
          "tpm": 8000,
          "tpd": 200000,
          "reset": "utc_midnight",
          "shared_with": "account",
          "observed": "Developer plan table; Free plan values to be measured in B4"
        },
        "data_terms": {
          "retention": "none_by_default",
          "human_review": false,
          "training": "no",
          "region_rules": [],
          "source_url": "https://console.groq.com/docs/your-data",
          "observed_at": "2026-10-28",
          "source_rating": "official",
          "summary": {
            "pl": "Groq domyślnie nie przechowuje treści zapytań; dzienniki tylko przy diagnozie lub nadużyciu, do 30 dni. Rozmowa idzie przez konto operatora tego serwera.",
            "en": "Groq does not retain request content by default; logs only for diagnosis or abuse, up to 30 days. The conversation goes through the account of this server's operator."
          }
        },
        "fallback_order": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "openrouter_free",
        "display_name": "OpenRouter (:free)",
        "base_url": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1",
        "adapter": "openai_compatible",
        "auth_env": "OPENROUTER_API_KEY",
        "auth_secret": "api_key",
        "tier": "free",
        "active_when": "key_present",
        "enabled": true,
        "models": [
          {
            "id": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free",
            "notes": "przykład / example"
          },
          {
            "id": "deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324:free",
            "notes": "przykład / example"
          }
        ],
        "limits": {
          "rpm": 20,
          "rpd": 50,
          "reset": "utc_midnight",
          "shared_with": "account",
          "observed": "50/day below 10 credits bought, 1000/day at >= 10; counter free_model_daily_requests in GET /api/v1/key"
        },
        "request_extra": {
          "provider": {
            "data_collection": "deny"
          }
        },
        "data_terms": {
          "retention": "depends_on_upstream",
          "human_review": "unspecified",
          "training": "no",
          "region_rules": [],
          "source_url": "https://openrouter.ai/docs/features/privacy-and-logging",
          "observed_at": "2026-10-28",
          "source_rating": "official",
          "summary": {
            "pl": "OpenRouter przekazuje zapytanie dostawcy modelu; konto operatora ma wyłączone kierowanie do dostawców uczących na danych, a zapytanie wymaga polityki bez zbierania danych (nazwa pola do potwierdzenia w B4).",
            "en": "OpenRouter forwards the request to a model host; the operator's account excludes hosts that train on data and the request asks for a no-data-collection policy (field name to be confirmed in B4)."
          }
        },
        "fallback_order": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "vertex_gemini",
        "display_name": "Google Vertex AI (Gemini)",
        "base_url": "https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/{project}/locations/global/endpoints/openapi",
        "adapter": "vertex_openai_compatible",
